// A `.map` whose callback arrives as a function-typed PARAMETER, with an f64 result, then an
// index read. `vl check` returns 0 and the emitter refuses with `emitProgram: index access
// but list type not collected` — clause 2. `collectMapFilterUse`'s result ladder has f64,
// i64 and f32 arms, but every one of them is behind `mfCallbackFe(...) >= 0`, which resolves
// a lifted function only; a parameter-delivered callback falls to the i32 default while the
// emitter still classifies the result as an f64 list.
// Should print 2.
function dbl(_n: i32): f64 { return 2.0 }
function go(f: (i32) => f64, xs: i32[]): f64 { return xs.map(f)[0] }
print(go(dbl, [1, 2]) as! i32)
